@startuml weight-ladder
' SPEC: _spec/apps/starchess/core/adjutant/weight-ladder.puml
' purpose: The Adjutant's scoring ladder — every named weight, its value, its
' tier, and which of the ordering invariants is actually enforced by a test.
' covers: packages/starchess-core/src/ai/strategies/survival.ts
' covers: packages/starchess-core/src/ai/strategies/captures.ts
' covers: packages/starchess-core/src/ai/strategies/checks.ts
' covers: packages/starchess-core/src/ai/strategies/mapControl.ts
' covers: packages/starchess-core/src/ai/strategies/economy.ts
' covers: packages/starchess-core/src/ai/context/posture.ts
' covers: packages/starchess-core/src/ai/strategic/strategies/checks.ts
' covers: packages/starchess-core/src/ai/strategic/strategies/runners.ts
' covers: packages/starchess-core/src/ai/strategic/strategies/attackers.ts
' covers: packages/starchess-core/src/ai/strategic/strategies/threats.ts
' covers: packages/starchess-core/src/ai/strategic/deployLookahead.ts
' covers: packages/starchess-core/src/__tests__/tactics/weightOrdering.test.ts
' see also: cc-focus.puml (which square the CC weights aim at)
' see also: strategic/promotion-defense.puml (the runner tiers in context)
' see also: strategic/cc-retaliation.puml (the retaliation tier in context)
' see also: strategic/strategic-economy.puml (the economy dials in context)
!include ../../../../themes/proveo.puml

skinparam packageStyle rectangle
skinparam defaultTextAlignment left

title StarChess · Adjutant weight ladder — one roster, one enforcing test

package "tiers, high to low" {
  component "**absolute survival**\nnever posture-scaled\n13_500 … 1_500" as T1 <<app>>
  component "**retaliation**\ntake what shot the CC\n9_000 (−40 × cost)" as T12 <<app>>
  component "**promotion race**\nstop an enemy runner\n7_000 … 600" as T15 <<app>>
  component "**Command Center pressure**\nstrategic checks + promotion rush\n6_000 … 450" as T2 <<app>>
  component "**material**\ncaptures / trades\n2_500 … 400" as T3 <<app>>
  component "**economy dials**\ndeploy mix + horizon\n3_500 … 600" as T4 <<app>>
  component "**posture weights**\nthe only contextual dial\n3_500 … 0" as T5 <<db>>
}

component "__tests__/tactics/weightOrdering.test.ts\n19 cases — the whole enforcement" as TEST <<async>>

T1 -[hidden]- T12
T12 -[hidden]- T15
T15 -[hidden]- T2
T2 -[hidden]- T3
T3 -[hidden]- T4
T4 -[hidden]- T5

TEST ARROW_MAIN T1 : 3 cases
TEST ARROW_MAIN T12 : 3 cases
TEST ARROW_MAIN T15 : 5 cases
TEST ARROW_MAIN T2 : 5 cases
TEST ARROW_MAIN T3 : 3 cases
TEST -[#CB2000,dashed]-> T4 : **no case** — unenforced
TEST -[#CB2000,dashed]-> T5 : **no case** — unenforced

note right of T1
  **Tier 1 — absolute survival** (""ai/strategies/survival.ts""):

  | weight | value | fires on |
  | ""DEPLOY_ATTACK_SURVIVAL"" | 13_500 (""KING_SAFETY + 3_500"") | deploy a unit, then take the checker with it |
  | ""KING_SAFETY"" | 10_000 | CC move to / from a safe square (signed) |
  | ""QUEEN_ESCAPE"" | 8_000 | Battleship under fire reaches safety |
  | ""BACKRANK_ESCAPE"" | 4_500 | threatened CC steps off its back rank |
  | ""QUEEN_WARP_CHECK_CC"" | 2_000 | Tactical Jump onto or beside the enemy CC |
  | ""DEFEND_UNIT"" | 1_800 | ordinary unit flees fire to safety |
  | ""QUEEN_THREAT_KING"" | 1_500 | enemy Battleship visible — CC prefers safety |

  These are the only weights the orchestrator never scales by posture, which
  is why the ladder is written from here down rather than from the top score.
end note

note as N_T2
  **Tier 2 — Command Center pressure.** Strategic
  (""ai/strategic/strategies/checks.ts"") replaces the naive pair wholesale;
  ""cc-focus.puml"" owns *which square* each one aims at:

  | weight | value | branch |
  | ""SNEAK_KNIGHT_CHECK_GUESS"" | 6_000 | fogged CC, ×0.5 when ""intel.strength == 0"" |
  | ""SNEAK_KNIGHT_CHECK_SEEN"" | 6_000 | visible CC |
  | ""PAWN_CHECK_CC_GUESS"" | 6_000 | fogged CC |
  | ""PAWN_CHECK_CC_SEEN"" | 6_000 | visible CC |
  | ""ATTACK_KING_GUESS"" | 5_000 | fogged CC, flat — replaces posture ""attackKing"" |
  | ""CHASE_KING_GUESS"" | 450 | fogged CC — equals hunt's ""chaseKing"", so chase is fog-neutral |
  | ""NEAR_PROMOTE_RUSH"" | 6_000 | ""ai/strategies/mapControl.ts"" — a Marine two steps from promotion |

  **Naive keeps its own, deliberately weaker pair** (""ai/strategies/checks.ts""):
  ""SNEAK_KNIGHT_CHECK"" 2_000 and ""PAWN_CHECK_CC"" 1_500. The strategic script
  is the one that is supposed to drive at the Command Center, so the gap is
  the difficulty setting rather than an oversight.
end note

note as N_T12
  **Tier 1.2 — retaliation** (""ai/strategic/strategies/attackers.ts""),
  strategic only. Full model in ""strategic/cc-retaliation.puml"":

  | weight | value | fires on |
  | ""AVENGE_CC_SHOT"" | 9_000 | a **capture** landing on a square something fired on our CC from |
  | ""AVENGE_THRIFT"" | 40 | × the answering unit's ""UNIT_COST"", subtracted |

  **It interleaves with tier 1 rather than sitting under it.** 9_000 is below
  ""KING_SAFETY"" 10_000 and ""DEPLOY_ATTACK_SURVIVAL"" 13_500, but *above*
  ""QUEEN_ESCAPE"" 8_000 — so the debt outbids saving the BattleShip, which the
  promotion race deliberately does not (invariant 12). Thrift only chooses
  *with what*: at 40 × 9 a BattleShip answer still keeps 8_640, above the tier
  below, so no unit can price itself out of the job.

  The deploy crush collects the same debt through ""avengeDeployValue"", which is
  why it is not a tier-4 dial — but it subtracts ""(trade + AVENGE_THRIFT) ×
  cost"", because the deploy loop's own ""trade × (1 + cost)"" otherwise out-runs
  a 40/cost thrift and makes the ring answer with the dearest unit it can
  afford. A thrift term on the deploy path must always be read against that
  slope (""strategic/cc-retaliation.puml"").
end note

note as N_T15
  **Tier 1.5 — the promotion race**
  (""ai/strategic/strategies/runners.ts""), strategic only; no naive twin
  exists, because naive reads promotion distance about *our* marines only.
  Full model in ""strategic/promotion-defense.puml"":

  | weight | value | fires on |
  | ""RUNNER_STOP_CRITICAL"" | 7_000 | enemy marine 1–2 squares out — it promotes on their next turn |
  | ""RUNNER_STOP_SERIOUS"" | 5_500 | 3–4 squares out — one turn of slack left |
  | ""RUNNER_STOP_WATCH"" | 600 | 5–6 squares out — a tie-break |

  The tier is multiplied by an **answer share** (capture 1 — 0.8 on a runner we
  only remember · block 0.8 · sidestep ×0.5 · hanging 0.3 · cover 0.35 ·
  abandon −0.8, waived when the blocker is fleeing fire), damped to 0.25
  while something already contains the runner, and scaled by the ghost's
  confidence when the runner is only remembered rather than seen
  (""runnerStake"" — see ""strategic/promotion-defense.puml"").
  ""RUNNER_SEEK_DAMP"" 0.25 is not
  a score but a **dial on tier 5**: while an urgent runner is on the board,
  ""buildStrategicCtx"" cuts ""seekFocus"", which is the one posture weight that
  multiplies per square and would otherwise out-bank any flat constant here.

  **Ally crush dials** (""ai/strategic/strategies/economy.ts"" deploy loop) —
  the Command Center may replace its own non-king ring units, so the victim is
  priced (mirror of the enemy-crush bonus) and only defense outbids an empty
  square:

  | weight | value | fires on |
  | ""ALLY_UPGRADE"" | 500 | ring full + defending + heavier guard replaces the cheapest ally in place |
  | ""ALLY_SHIELD_PAWN"" | 800 | fresh cover from the crush square onto a lit, threatened own near-promotion pawn (cheap victim, sole blockers exempt) |
  | ""ALLY_SHIELD_SHIP"" | 1_200 | same cover onto a lit, threatened own ship |

  Each dial — and their sum — sits below ""RUNNER_STOP_SERIOUS"": only
  ""runnerDeployValue"" itself (already laddered) can lift an ally-crush into
  the runner tiers, never the dials alone.

  Placement between tiers 1 and 2 is the deliberate claim: the last turn on
  which a promotion can be stopped outranks a check we could repeat, but never
  outranks saving the BattleShip or the Command Center.
end note

note as N_T34
  **Tier 3 — material** (""ai/strategies/captures.ts""):

  | weight | value | fires on |
  | ""CHARON_COMBO"" | 2_500 | Charon strike, then a second unit acts the same turn |
  | ""EQUAL_TRADE_ATTACK"" | 2_400 | equal-material capture in range |
  | ""SAC_FOR_CC_WINNING"" | 1_800 | give a unit to keep the enemy CC under fire, while ahead |
  | ""HUNT_UNDEFENDED_PAWN"" | 950 | take a Marine no unit **and no deploy** covers |
  | ""PAWN_TRADE"" | 750 | Marine-for-Marine while congested |
  | ""SAC_FOR_CC"" | 400 | the same sacrifice while only level |

  ""undefended"" is decided by ""deploy-reach.puml"", not by unit attacks alone —
  a square the enemy could recapture with a deploy is defended.

  **Tier 4 — economy dials.** Naive (""ai/strategies/economy.ts""):
  ""BISHOP_VS_QUEEN"" 3_500 · ""BISHOP_FIRST"" 2_200 · ""ROOK_AFTER_KNIGHTS"" 900 ·
  ""MAX_KNIGHTS"" 2 (a cap, not a weight). Strategic
  (""ai/strategic/strategies/economy.ts""): ""QUEEN_FINISH"" 3_200 ·
  ""HIDDEN_GUARD"" 1_450 · ""RUNNER_GUARD"" 1_450 · ""SHIP_WARP_READY"" 800, plus
  ""SHIP_HORIZON_BONUS"" 600 over ""HORIZON"" 5 from ""deployLookahead.ts"". The two
  guards are equal today and deliberately separate: they fire on different
  evidence (hidden material vs a runner we can account for), and the tank
  collects one or the other, never both.
end note

note as N_T5
  **Tier 5 — posture weights** (""ai/context/posture.ts""). The only contextual
  dial; a strategy reads them and never branches on the posture name:

  | weight | expand | seek | hunt |
  | ""siegeHub"" | 1_200 | 950 | 180 |
  | ""mapControl"" | 800 | 480 | 140 |
  | ""diagonal"" | 400 | 360 | 280 |
  | ""promoteRank"" | 0 | 60 | 100 |
  | ""promotionBonus"" | 0 | 420 | 700 |
  | ""attackKing"" | 0 | 0 | 3_500 |
  | ""chaseKing"" | 0 | 0 | 450 |
  | ""seekFocus"" | 0 | 700 | 0 |
  | ""center"" | 50 | 30 | 25 |
  | ""trade"" | 100 | 100 | 120 |
  | ""attackedPenalty"" | 400 | 400 | 400 |

  ""hunt"" requires a visible enemy CC, so ""attackKing"" and ""chaseKing"" are
  **structurally zero** on any turn the CC is fogged. A guess branch therefore
  never competes with them, which is why ""ATTACK_KING_GUESS"" exists as a flat
  constant instead of a posture row.
end note

T12 .. N_T12
T15 .. N_T15
T2 .. N_T2
T3 .. N_T34
T5 .. N_T5

note bottom of TEST
  **The ladder is a sum, not a selection.** The orchestrator adds every
  strategy's score for a move, so an ordering between two constants only
  decides the outcome when nothing else contributes. Two weights that stack on
  one move can beat a higher tier, which is how the Marine double-count in
  ""cc-focus.puml"" inverts an invariant this file's test still passes — twice
  over now: that stack is 11_000 effective, so it also outbids tier 1.2
  retaliation at 9_000 (""strategic/cc-retaliation.puml"" records the exception).

  **The eighteen enforced invariants**, over 19 cases — invariant 4 is asserted
  twice, once stacked and once bare. They used to be prose beside the constants
  ("must outrank mapControl (e2 5104 vs c2 102)"), where nothing checked them
  and a retune could silently invert them:

  | # | invariant |
  | 1 | every tier-1.5/2/3 weight < ""KING_SAFETY"" (14 constants swept) |
  | 2 | ""DEPLOY_ATTACK_SURVIVAL"" > ""KING_SAFETY"" > ""BACKRANK_ESCAPE"" |
  | 3 | ""QUEEN_ESCAPE"" > ""DEFEND_UNIT"" and > ""QUEEN_THREAT_KING"" |
  | 4 | ""PAWN_CHECK_CC_GUESS"" ≥ ""NEAR_PROMOTE_RUSH"" — the old comment's claim |
  | 5 | both sneak weights > ""EQUAL_TRADE_ATTACK"" |
  | 6 | ""SNEAK_KNIGHT_CHECK_SEEN"" > naive ""SNEAK_KNIGHT_CHECK"" |
  | 7 | ""SAC_FOR_CC_WINNING"" < ""EQUAL_TRADE_ATTACK"" |
  | 8 | ""SAC_FOR_CC"" < ""SAC_FOR_CC_WINNING"" |
  | 9 | ""SAC_FOR_CC"" < ""HUNT_UNDEFENDED_PAWN"" |
  | 10 | every guess weight ≤ its seen twin |
  | 11 | ""RUNNER_STOP_CRITICAL"" > both *seen* check weights — the last chance to stop a promotion beats a repeatable check |
  | 12 | ""RUNNER_STOP_CRITICAL"" < ""QUEEN_ESCAPE"" — and so below all of tier 1 |
  | 13 | ""RUNNER_STOP_SERIOUS"" > ""ATTACK_KING_GUESS"" and > ""EQUAL_TRADE_ATTACK"" — a real runner beats speculation and beats ordinary material |
  | 14 | ""RUNNER_STOP_SERIOUS"" < both *guess* check weights — a real check still wins the turn |
  | 15 | ""RUNNER_STOP_WATCH"" < ""HUNT_UNDEFENDED_PAWN"" — a distant runner is a tie-break, not a plan |
  | 16 | ""AVENGE_CC_SHOT"" < ""KING_SAFETY"" and < ""DEPLOY_ATTACK_SURVIVAL"" — the CC's own safety outranks avenging it |
  | 17 | ""AVENGE_CC_SHOT"" > every other concern the turn offers (6 constants swept, ""QUEEN_ESCAPE"" included) |
  | 18 | ""AVENGE_CC_SHOT"" − ""AVENGE_THRIFT"" × 9 > ""RUNNER_STOP_CRITICAL"" — even spending a BattleShip, thrift never refuses the job |
  | 19 | ""ALLY_UPGRADE"" / ""ALLY_SHIELD_PAWN"" / ""ALLY_SHIELD_SHIP"" each < ""RUNNER_STOP_SERIOUS"", and ""ALLY_SHIELD_SHIP"" + ""ALLY_UPGRADE"" < ""RUNNER_STOP_SERIOUS"" — ally-crush dials nudge, never outbid a real runner tier |
  | 20 | ""ALLY_SHIELD_SHIP"" + ""ALLY_UPGRADE"" < ""RUNNER_STOP_CRITICAL"" and ""ALLY_SHIELD_SHIP"" < ""AVENGE_CC_SHOT"" — ally dials alone never reach the last-chance tier or retaliation |

  Invariant 4 is the tightest in the ladder: 6_000 ≥ 6_000 holds by equality,
  so any cut to the Marine check breaks it immediately. That is deliberate —
  the point of the case is that a check must never lose to a quiet promotion
  square. It runs in ""pnpm ci"" through ""test:packages"".
end note

note as N_GAPS
  **What no test pins.** Tiers 4 and 5 have no ordering case at all, so a
  deploy dial may drift past a survival weight without anything failing.
  ""KNIGHT_1_MOVE_BLOCK"" 800 and ""KNIGHT_1_MOVE_KING_STEP"" 600 in
  ""ai/strategic/strategies/threats.ts"" are module-private and cannot be
  asserted from outside at all.

  **The rule those two weights encode.** An enemy Hoverbike standing on
  ""tactical.checkThreatSquares"" will deliver check next turn unless we move the
  Command Center or put something in the way, so strategic ""threats"" rewards
  acting a turn early rather than waiting to be checked. A Hoverbike cannot be
  blocked on a ray, so the only real interposition is a unit that lands adjacent
  to our own CC and can take it — which is why the reward tests CC adjacency
  rather than ray membership. Both weights are held **below** the offensive
  check tier on purpose: a defensive nudge must never outbid a real check.

  <color:#CB2000>**OPEN**</color> — ""KNIGHT_1_MOVE_KING_STEP"" is **dead**.
  ""threats.ts"" returns 0 on ""isKingMove"" at the top of ""score"", so the
  ""isKingMove"" branch further down can never run. The CC-step half of the rule
  above is therefore unimplemented, while the interpose half does fire. The
  comment that claimed the balance held quoted 3_000 / 5_000 for the offensive
  weights, which have since become 6_000 / 5_000 — the ordering survived the
  retune, but nothing checked that it did.
end note

TEST .. N_GAPS
@enduml
